\ls1\ilvl1{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Because there is no shared clock, each component works independent of the other; the bits sent must match timing derived from a pre-agreed baud rate.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Full-duplex: lines are TX and RX which are separate (transmit - receive) (allows for separate communication)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Frame-based (data is sent in frames wrapped in start/stop bits allowing receiver to detect boundaries w/o clock)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Saying UART typically refers to the hardware peripheral (chip / IP) converting parallel data from CPU into a serial bitstream, or the other way around\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Some UART implementations add hardware flow control lines:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}RTS and CTS which are used to prevent buffer overruns\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Buffer overruns happen when one device cannot keep up with the other\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
