\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}UART Frame:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Since there is no clock line, UART is entirely frame-based. Start/stops are transmitted as voltage levels on the wire using a fixed frame format\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}A single frame:\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li2160\fi-2160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Idle (line sits HIGH)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Start bit (line is pulled low for a single bit period)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Data bits (5-9, most commonly 8, w/ the LSB sent first)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Parity bit (error-check bit that can be even, odd, or none)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Stop bit (line returns HIGH for 1 or 2 bit periods, marking end of the frame)\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Frames are often written in shorthand: 8N1 - 8 data, no parity, 1 stop\
